# LAYER 11 — THE 24-HOUR RULE

The user's requirement is:

> No stale data older than 24 hours.

Implement this intelligently.

Do NOT blindly reject every piece of data older than 24 hours.

Instead use **data-class-specific freshness policies**.

Example:

| Data | Policy |
|---|---|
| Intraday stock price | LIVE |
| Intraday volume | LIVE |
| Market breadth | Current session |
| Current news | Preferably minutes/hours |
| Daily close | Latest trading session |
| ETF NAV | Latest official |
| Mutual fund NAV | Latest official |
| Quarterly earnings | Latest official filing |
| Annual report | Latest official report |
| GDP | Latest official release |
| Inflation | Latest official release |
| Central bank decision | Latest official decision |

Hard rule:

> Never present stale data as current.

